# ======================================================================
# cookbook.agg  --  insurance-useful worked examples (shipped)
# ======================================================================
#
# PURPOSE
# -------
# The broad, insurance-flavoured companion to examples.agg. Where
# examples.agg is the small curated public set (the default `build`
# knowledge base, the 20-minute intro, the SPA dropdown), cookbook.agg is
# the larger reference of worked recipes: near-complete DecL feature
# coverage shown on realistic books -- every severity and frequency
# family, mixing, splicing, all reinsurance forms, signed / P&L support,
# the pnl and bivariate keywords, method-of-moments approximation,
# windowed sizing, the distortion constructors, and book/paper
# reproductions. Referenced from the docs; intended to ship at v1.0.
#
# Sibling shipped libraries: examples.agg (curated default),
# actuarial-severity-curves.agg (severity reference), decl-testers.agg
# (language stress).
#
# STATUS: DRAFT. Seeded from the legacy feature walkthrough; still to be
# de-duplicated and the section/naming scheme finalized (expect a few
# duplicate names until that curation pass). Target ~128-256 lines.
#
# FORMAT: same DecL line format as examples.agg. note{} is legal on
# agg/sev/port/pnl/bv lines, not on dist lines (use "#" comments there).
# ======================================================================

# Default severity used in many other examples
sev One dsev [1]

# Guides examples
# ===============

# Simple Dice Examples
# =====================
agg A.Dice00 dfreq [1:6] dsev [1] note{The roll of a single dice as frequency.};
agg A.Dice01 dfreq [1] dsev [1:6] note{The roll of a single dice as severity.};
agg A.Dice02 dfreq [2] dsev [1:6] note{Sum of the rolls of two dice.};
agg A.Dice03 dfreq [5] dsev [1:6] note{Sum of the rolls of five dice.};
agg A.Basic01 dfreq [12] dsev [0 1] note{toss of 12 coins};
agg A.Basic02 dfreq [12] dsev [-1 1] note{12 step random walk};
agg A.Basic03 dfreq [1:3] dsev [1 2 10] note{1, 2 or 3 claims using range notation, sev 1, 2, 10 all equally likely};
agg A.Basic06 dfreq [1:3] [.5 1/4 1/4] dsev [1 2 10] [.4 .4 .2] note{1, 2 or 3 claims; severity 1, 2 or 10 each with specified probabilities };
agg A.Basic07 dfreq [0 1 2] [.5 .3 .2] sev.One note{Using a built in severity}


# Frequency distributions
agg A.Fixed 10 claims sev.One fixed note{fixed claim count};
agg A.Poisson 10 claims sev.One poisson note{Poisson claim count};
agg A.Bernoulli .8 claims sev.One bernoulli note{Bernoulli claim count};
agg A.Binomial 10 claims sev.One binomial 0.5 note{binomial n=10, p=1/2 claim count};
agg A.Geometric 10 claims sev.One geometric note{geometric claim count};
agg A.NegBin 10 claims sev.One negbin 3 note{negative binomial; shape parameter 3 equals variance multiplier};
# Mixing distributions
agg A.NegBinMix 10 claims sev.One mixed gamma 0.65 note{negative binomial as gamma mixed Poisson, shape parameter equals cv of mixing distribution};
agg A.IG 10 claims sev.One mixed ig .65 note{inverse Gaussian mixing distribution};
# ZM and ZT distributions, note alternative way to specify fixed severity
agg A.ZM-Poisson 4 claims dsev [1] poisson zt note{zero truncated Poisson with mean 4};
agg A.ZT-Poisson 4 claims dsev [1] poisson zm .5 note{zero modified Poisson}

# Severity only, fixed freq, different distributions
# ==================================================
# zero parameter
agg D.Sev01 1 claim sev 100 * expon fixed note{scaled exponential};
agg D.Sev03 1 claim sev 100 * expon + 10 fixed note{scaled and shifted exponential};
agg D.Sev04 1 claim ssev 100 * norm + 50 fixed note{signed severity, scaled and shifted normal};
# one parameter
agg D.Sev06 1 claim sev 10 * gamma 0.3 fixed note{scaled gamma with shape};
agg D.Sev07 1 claim sev gamma 12 cv .3 fixed note{gamma by mean and cv};
agg D.Sev08 1 claim sev lognorm 50 cv .3 fixed note{lognormal by mean and cv};
# TODO(merge): legacy reversed-severity syntax `sev - lognorm` no longer parses; restate with the modern reflect form.
# agg D.Sev08 1 claim sev - lognorm 50 cv .3 fixed note{reversed lognormal}
agg D.Sev09 1 claim sev 50/exp(.3**2/2) * lognorm .3 fixed note{mean equals 50 and cv is slightly higher than .3};
agg D.Sev10 1 claim sev 100 * invgamma 4.07 fixed note{remember must set scale or mean};
agg D.Sev11 1 claim sev 100 * weibull_min 1.5 fixed;
agg D.Sev12 1 claim sev invgauss 10 cv .5 fixed;
agg D.Sev13 1 claim sev 10 * pareto 2.6 - 10 fixed note{Standard Pareto, support >= 0};
# two parameter distributions
agg D.Sev14 1 claim sev 50 * beta 3 2 + 10 fixed note{50*beta(3,2) + 10};
# limits, attachments, and unconditional
agg E.TSev15 5 claims 200 xs 0 sev 1.2343e2 * lognorm 2 poisson note{conditional severity};
agg E.TSev16 5 claims 200 xs 0 sev 1.2343e2 * lognorm 2 ! poisson note{unconditional severity};
agg E.TSev17 5 claims 200 xs 10 sev 1.2343e2 * lognorm 2 poisson note{conditional severity};
agg E.TSev18 5 claims 200 xs 10 sev 1.2343e2 * lognorm 2 ! poisson note{unconditional severity};
# spliced
agg T.Splice01 1 claim sev lognorm 10 cv .5 splice [5 20] fixed note{lognormal conditional on 5 <= X <= 20}

# Specifying exposure
# ===================
agg F.Expos01 10 claims sev lognorm 50 cv 0.8 poisson note{specify number of claims};
agg F.Expos02 500 loss sev lognorm 50 cv 0.8 poisson note{specify expected loss, derive number of claims};
agg F.Expos03 1000 prem at .5 lr sev lognorm 50 cv 0.8 poisson note{specify premium and loss ratio, derive number of claims}

# Mixed and Spliced severities
# ============================
agg G.Mixed09 8 claims sev 100 * [lognorm expon] [.5 1] wts [0.6 .4] mixed gamma 0.3 note{mixture of severities};
agg H.Limits01 [5 10 8 2] claims [1 5 10 20] xs 0 sev lognorm 10 cv 1.2 mixed gamma 0.2 note{limit profile, single severity};
agg I.Blend09 [1000 2000 500] prem at [.8 .7 .5] lr sev lognorm 10 cv [.35 .5] wts [5/8 3/8] mixed gamma 0.5 note{limit profile and mixed severity} hints{log2=17;}

# Reinsurance
# ===========
agg J.Re01 5 claims 120 xs 0 sev 120 * uniform occurrence net of 50% so 25 xs 25 and 90% po 50 xs 50 poisson note{occurrence reinsurance; note over the top exposure};
agg J.Re01 5 claims 120 xs 0 sev 120 * uniform poisson aggregate net of 100 xs 240 note{aggregate reinsurance};
agg J.Re01 5 claims 120 xs 0 sev 120 * uniform occurrence ceded to 60 xs 60 poisson aggregate ceded to 180 xs 0 note{occurrence with an aggregate limit}


# Tweedie distributions
# =====================
agg K.Tweedie0 10.050251256281404 claims sev gamma 0.0995 cv 0.07088812050083283 poisson note{Tweedie defined by claim count, gamma mean and cv};
agg K.Tweedie1 10.050251256281404 claims sev 0.0005 * gamma 199 poisson note{Tweedie defined by claim count, gamma scale and shape};
agg K.Tweedie2 tweedie 1 1.005 0.1 note{Tweedie defined using mean, p, and dispersion, variance = dispersion xs mean**p}

# Examples from books and papers
# ==============================
port L.Bodoff1 note{Bodoff Thought Experiment No. 1} agg wind1 1 claim sev dhistogram xps [0, 99] [0.80, 0.20] fixed agg quake1 1 claim sev dhistogram xps [0, 100] [0.95, 0.05] fixed;
port L.Bodoff1N note{Bodoff Thought Experiment No. 1} agg wind1 1 claim dsev [0, 99] [0.80, 0.20] fixed agg quake1 1 claim dsev [0, 100] [0.95, 0.05] fixed

port L.Bodoff2 note{Bodoff Thought Experiment No. 2} agg wind2 1 claim sev dhistogram xps [0, 50] [0.80, 0.20] fixed agg quake2 1 claim sev dhistogram xps [0, 100] [0.95, 0.05] fixed;
port L.Bodoff2N note{Bodoff Thought Experiment No. 2} agg wind2 1 claim dsev [0, 50] [0.80, 0.20] fixed agg quake2 1 claim dsev [0, 100] [0.95, 0.05] fixed

port L.Bodoff3 note{Bodoff Thought Experiment No. 3} agg wind3 1 claim sev dhistogram xps [0, 5] [0.80, 0.20] fixed agg quake3 1 claim sev dhistogram xps [0, 100] [0.95, 0.05] fixed;
port L.Bodoff3N note{Bodoff Thought Experiment No. 3} agg wind3 1 claim sev dhistogram xps [0, 5] [0.80, 0.20] fixed agg quake3 1 claim sev dhistogram xps [0, 100] [0.95, 0.05] fixed

port M.PIR.Discrete note{PIR Discrete case study.} agg Discrete.X1 1 claim dsev [0 8 10] [1/2 1/4 1/4] fixed agg Discrete.X2 1 claim dsev [0 1 90] [1/2 1/4 1/4] fixed hints{bs=1; log2=8; padding=1}

port M.PIR.Tame note{PIR Tame case study. For reinsurance see text.} agg Tame.A 1 claim sev gamma 50 cv 0.10 fixed agg Tame.B 1 claim sev gamma 50 cv 0.15 fixed hints{bs=1/64; log2=16; padding=1}

port M.PIR.CNC.Gross note{PIR Cat-Noncat gross case study.} agg CNC.NonCat 1 claim sev gamma 80 cv 0.15 fixed agg CNC.Cat 1 claim sev lognorm 20 cv 1.00 fixed hints{bs=1/64; log2=16; padding=1};
port M.PIR.CNC.Net note{PIR Cat-Noncat net case study.} agg CNC.Net.NonCat 1 claim sev gamma 80 cv 0.15 fixed agg CNC.Net.Cat 1 claim sev lognorm 20 cv 1.00 fixed aggregate net of 79.64 xs 41.11 hints{bs=1/64; log2=16; padding=1}



agg P.Def.Pareto 1 claim sev 1000 * pareto 1.5 - 1000 fixed note{defective; no finite 2nd moment} hints{normalize=False}





# W. Distortion DecL constructors
# ===============================
# Combo distortions (minimum, mixture) reference child distortions by name
# via ``dist.X`` / ``distortion.X`` (tests/test_distortion_construction.py).
# Both prefixes resolve through the knowledge base.
#
# Leaf distortions are live and validated by interpret_file. The four combo
# lines below are commented out because interpret_file() parses each line
# with a fresh, empty knowledge base — combo lookups need the children
# already registered, which only happens through a sequential file load
# (Underwriter.load). They are listed verbatim for reference; uncomment when
# loading via Underwriter.load.
dist CCoC-distortion ccoc .25;
dist PH-distortion ph 0.65;
dist Wang-distortion ph 0.7;
dist Dual-distortion dual 2.5;
dist TVaR-distortion tvar 0.4


# P&L. Negative-support (signed) severity and the output window (1.0.0a21)
# =======================================================================
# Drive negative-x: a profit is a negative loss. dsev with a negative atom
# auto-signs; continuous P&L severities use the ssev keyword (the never-clamp
# sibling of sev). A signed aggregate auto-windows from build/update (x_min
# defaults to 'auto' -> a two-sided window); a number forces the origin. See
# tests/test_negative_x.py and dev/plan-negative-x-agg.md.
agg PnL.Fix dfreq [3] dsev [-2 5] [.5 .5] note{fixed-3; closed form support (-6,1,8,15)};
agg PnL.SD dfreq [3] dsev [-1 1] note{zero-mean signed; sev SD 1, agg SD sqrt(3) -- derived from ex2, not mean*cv};
agg PnL.Sym 20 claims dsev [-1 1] [.5 .5] poisson note{symmetric P&L; mean 0};
agg PnL.Lump 1e6 claims dsev [-1 10] [15/16 1/16] poisson note{near-Gaussian lump at a negative mean ~ -312500; auto window};
agg PnL.Norm 100 claims ssev 50 * norm + 10 poisson note{continuous signed (ssev) P&L severity; never clamps};
agg PnL.PmL 5 claims ssev 100 - lognorm 80 cv .2 poisson note{premium minus loss: constant - dist reflects the severity (sev mean 20)}


# PortPnL. Portfolio combine on signed (P&L) support (1.0.0a22)
# ============================================================
# Independent signed units combine onto a shared signed grid: the FFT product
# is origin-at-0 (ftagg_density is independent of each unit's x_min) and a
# single F2 roll places the total on [x_min_tot, ...]. Comparable-scale units
# share one bs so the combine is exact (means add, variances add). A signed +
# ordinary mix straddles 0. Pricing columns (add_exa) are deferred -> F/S only.
# See tests/test_negative_x_port.py and dev/plan-negative-x-port.md.
port PortPnL.Pair agg A 50 claims ssev 10 * norm + 5 poisson agg B 50 claims ssev 10 * norm - 5 poisson;
port sev-vs-ssev agg A 50 claims ssev 10 * norm + 5 poisson agg B 50 claims ssev 10 * norm - 5 poisson;
port PortPnL.Mixed agg Loss 30 claims sev lognorm 20 cv 0.8 poisson agg PnL 50 claims ssev 10 * norm poisson

port Gotcha agg A 50 claims sev 10 * norm + 5 splice [0 40] poisson agg B 50 claims sev 10 * norm - 5 splice [0 35] poisson

# ============================================================
# PnLprem. The pnl keyword: premium-minus-loss aggregates (1.0.0a23)
# ============================================================
# pnl NAME <premium> prem - <loss body> builds an ordinary loss aggregate and
# applies an aggregate-level affine wrapper PnL = premium - A (reflect + a
# single shift by the total premium). The premium is subtracted ONCE for the
# book (unlike a constant inside sev/ssev, which is per-claim). value_type is
# set to payoff. Three exposure heads: N% lr (binds to the premium), N claims,
# N loss. The premium vectorises like an agg exposure (total pnl only). A pnl
# line goes anywhere an agg does, including as a port unit. See tests/test_pnl.py
# and dev/done/plan-pnl-premium.md.
pnl PnLprem.LR 1000 prem - 70% lr sev lognorm 100 cv 2 poisson note{loss ratio form: E[loss]=700, margin 300};
pnl PnLprem.Claims 100 prem - 10 claims sev lognorm 8 cv 1.5 poisson note{claims form: premium independent of the loss model};
pnl PnLprem.Loss 100 prem - 85 loss sev lognorm 8 cv 1.5 poisson note{expected-loss form: E[loss]=85, margin 15};
pnl PnLprem.Vec [100 200 100] prem - .8 lr [1000 2000 5000] xs 0 sev lognorm 500 cv 2 poisson note{vector premium: shift 400, mean 80 = sum premium_i (1-lr)};
port PnLprem.Book pnl Cat 2000 prem - 55% lr sev lognorm 500 cv 3 poisson pnl Prop 5000 prem - 65% lr sev lognorm 100 cv 2 poisson;
# Signed loss severity (dsev negative atom / ssev) under pnl (1.0.0a45): the
# loss convolves on its genuine signed grid before the affine relabel. See
# tests/test_pnl.py and dev/done/plan-pnl-signed-severity.md.
pnl PnLsigned.Dsev 5 premium - dfreq[3] dsev[-1 1] note{signed loss: PnL in (2,4,6,8), mean 5, sd sqrt3};
pnl PnLsigned.Asym 10 premium - dfreq[2] dsev[-2 1 3] [.5 .3 .2] note{non-symmetric signed dsev: mean = 10 - 2 E[X] = 10.2};
pnl PnLsigned.Ssev 100 premium - 5 claims ssev 20 - lognorm 10 cv 0.5 poisson note{continuous signed severity: E[loss]=50, margin 50}

# ============================================================
# MV. The bivariate keyword: copula-coupled aggregates (1.0.0a24)
# ============================================================
# bivariate NAME <shared-count> <two agg/pnl components> copula KIND P [freq]
# couples the two components' per-claim severities by a copula and accumulates
# them with a shared outer frequency via a 2D FFT. Each component's dfreq [0 1]
# [p0 p1] is the per-event trigger; its aggregate is the per-event severity
# g_i = (1-p_i) delta_0 + p_i f_i. Marginalising one axis reproduces that
# component's standalone aggregate. A pnl component contributes its loss
# severity and applies the premium as a per-axis affine after the FFT (the
# loss-loss copula dependence becomes profit-loss). Copulas (aggregate.copula):
# normal (Pearson rho), gumbel (Kendall tau), clayton (Kendall tau), fgm
# (Spearman rho_s), independent; t is deferred. See tests/test_bivariate.py
# and dev/plan-mv.md.
# Programs are one-per-line (DecL is whitespace-insensitive within a program).
bivariate MV.Gumbel 25 claims agg Wind dfreq [0 1] [.3 .7] sev lognorm 40 cv 1.2 agg Flood dfreq [0 1] [.5 .5] sev lognorm 60 cv 1.5 copula gumbel 0.4 poisson;
bivariate MV.ClaytonMixed 25 claims agg Wind dfreq [0 1] [.3 .7] sev lognorm 40 cv 1.2 agg Flood dfreq [0 1] [.5 .5] sev lognorm 60 cv 1.5 copula clayton 0.3 mixed gamma .2;
bivariate MV.Normal 25 claims agg A dfreq [0 1] [.5 .5] sev lognorm 50 cv 1.5 agg B dfreq [0 1] [.5 .5] sev gamma 50 cv 1.0 copula normal 0.5;
bivariate MV.PnLAxis 25 claims agg A dfreq [0 1] [.3 .7] sev lognorm 40 cv 1.2 pnl B 900 prem - dfreq [0 1] [.5 .5] sev lognorm 60 cv 1.5 copula gumbel 0.4 poisson;
bivariate MV.Indep 25 claims agg A dfreq [0 1] [.5 .5] sev lognorm 50 cv 1.5 agg B dfreq [0 1] [.5 .5] sev gamma 50 cv 1.0 poisson;
# netceded MODE: the joint (ceded, net) occurrence law of one reinsured aggregate
# (same object as Aggregate.occ_bivariate()). Body is an ordinary agg carrying
# occurrence reinsurance; the two axes are Ceded and Net.
netceded agg MV.NetCeded 8 claims sev 300 * beta 2 3 occurrence net of 0.7 so 60 xs 40 poisson


# ============================================================
# APX. Method-of-moments approximation keyword (1.0.0a47)
# ============================================================
# `approximate sgamma | slognorm` replaces the freq x sev convolution, at
# construction, with a single continuous severity fitted to the aggregate's
# first three moments (shifted gamma / shifted lognormal; normal as the
# symmetric limit; a reflected fit for left skew), carried on a fixed frequency
# of 1. `exact` (or omitting the clause) is the inert default. Incompatible with
# occurrence reinsurance (the fit bypasses the per-occurrence convolution);
# aggregate reinsurance rides along. See tests/test_approximate.py and
# dev/done/plan-approximate.md.
agg APX.RightSgamma 5000 claim sev lognorm 100 cv 2 poisson approximate sgamma;
agg APX.RightSlognorm 5000 claim sev lognorm 100 cv 2 poisson approximate slognorm;
agg APX.LeftReflect 1 claim sev 100 * beta 5 1.3 fixed approximate sgamma;
agg APX.AggReins 100 claim sev lognorm 100 cv 2 poisson aggregate net of 100 xs 0 approximate sgamma;
pnl APX.PnL 600000 prem - 5000 claim sev lognorm 100 cv 2 poisson approximate sgamma

# ============================================================
# WIN. Non-zero aggregate output window -- windowed sizing (1.0.0a51)
# ============================================================
# A concentrated aggregate (agg_cv < 1/z, mass band clears 0) is computed on a
# two-sided window far from 0 via benign FFT wrap: bs sizes off the band width,
# not x_max, so a high-mean book resolves finely with a non-zero x_min. Window
# is the headline 10M-claim integer case (resolves at bs=1); WinCts is the
# continuous analogue. See tests/test_bucket_sizing.py and
# dev/done/plan-bucket-window.md.
agg Window 10000000 claims dsev [1 2] poisson;
agg WinCts 100000 claims sev lognorm 100 cv 0.5 poisson

# N3. Distortion spine (numerics-3)
# =================================
# Programs behind tests/test_numerics3_distortion.py (1.0.0a57): the exact-
# discrete Choquet helper, the view x value_type 2x2, the unified linear/
# lifted builder, builder-level mass guard, signed total pricing, and the
# on-demand per-line capital. See dev/done/plan-numerics-3-distortion.md.
agg N3.Dice dfreq [1:6] dsev [1:6] note{six-surface consistency target; choquet hand checks};
port N3.OneDice agg D dfreq [1:6] dsev [1:6] note{one-line port: line == total};
port N3.Bodoff agg wind 1 claim sev dhistogram xps [0, 99] [0.80, 0.20] fixed agg quake 1 claim sev dhistogram xps [0, 100] [0.95, 0.05] fixed note{bounded discrete; linear vs lifted; mass distortion exact};
port N3.SignedD agg A dfreq [1 2] dsev [-3 -1 2] [.5 .3 .2] agg B dfreq [1] dsev [-2 1 4] agg C dfreq [2] dsev [1 3] note{signed totals price via dot(kappa, gp); shares NaN};
port N3.PayPair pnl P1 10 prem - dfreq [1] dsev [2 5] [.5 .5] pnl P2 8 prem - dfreq [1] dsev [1 3] note{homogeneous payoff book prices through the dual};
port N3.Unb agg U 5 claims sev lognorm 10 cv 1 poisson note{mass-on-unbounded refused in the lifted builder (G6)}


# ======================================================================
# Z. Harvested from spa_examples.agg (provisional -- de-duplicate in curation)
# ======================================================================
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# A. Aggregates -- getting started
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
agg A.ThreeDice dfreq [3] dsev [1:6] note{Sum of the rolls of three dice.};
agg A.DiceDice dfreq [1:6] dsev [1:6] note{Roll a die for the claim count, then sum that many die rolls.};
agg A.Basic 15 claims 10000 xs 0 sev lognorm 1500 cv 1.0 poisson note{A plain Poisson / lognormal aggregate.}

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# B. Portfolios
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
port B.BasicPort agg A 50 claims 1000 xs 0 sev lognorm 100 cv 1.2 mixed gamma 0.4 agg B 65 claims 2000 xs 0 sev lognorm 150 cv 1.6 mixed gamma 0.2 note{Two-unit portfolio.};
port B.PnLPort pnl Cat 2000 prem - 55% lr sev lognorm 500 cv 3 poisson pnl Prop 5000 prem - 65% lr sev lognorm 100 cv 2 poisson note{Portfolio of two profit-and-loss units.}

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# C. Reinsurance
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
agg C.BasicXOL 15 claims 10000 xs 0 sev lognorm 1500 cv 1.0 occurrence net of 50% po 2500 xs 2500 and 90% po 5000 xs 5000 mixed gamma 0.25 note{Occurrence excess-of-loss program, net view.};
agg C.Reins 1250 premium at 80% lr 1000 xs 0 sev lognorm 80 cv 1.675 occurrence ceded to 125 xs 0 and 50% po 125 xs 125 and 20% po 250 xs 250 and 5% po 500 xs 500 poisson note{Layered occurrence reinsurance, ceded view.}

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# D. Multivariate and dependent risks
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
bv D.Cat 25 claims agg Wind dfreq [0 1] [.3 .7] sev lognorm 40 cv 0.65 splice [0 250] agg Flood dfreq [0 1] [.5 .5] sev lognorm 60 cv 0.95 splice [0 300] mixed gamma .2 note{Common-shock bivariate (bv): Wind and Flood share frequency mixing.};
netceded agg D.NetCeded 15 claims 10000 xs 0 sev lognorm 1500 cv 1.0 occurrence net of 50% po 2500 xs 2500 and 90% po 5000 xs 5000 mixed gamma 0.25 note{Gross / ceded / net joint view of a reinsured book.};
bivariate D.MVGumbel 25 claims agg Wind dfreq [0 1] [.3 .7] sev lognorm 40 cv 1.2 agg Flood dfreq [0 1] [.5 .5] sev lognorm 60 cv 1.5 copula gumbel 0.4 poisson note{Gumbel-copula dependence between Wind and Flood.}

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# E. Profit and loss
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
pnl E.PNL 1000 prem - 90% lr 1000 xs 0 sev lognorm 120 cv 1 mixed gamma .25 note{Single profit-and-loss line.};
pnl E.PnLMix [100 200 100] prem - .8 lr [1000 2000 5000] xs 0 sev lognorm 500 cv 2 poisson note{Vector premium: shift 400, mean 80 = sum premium_i (1 - lr).}

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# F. Severity and frequency features
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
agg F.MixedMixed [5 10 8 2] claims [1 5 10 20] xs 0 sev lognorm 10 cv 1.2 mixed gamma 0.2 note{Limit profile, single severity.};
agg F.Tweedie tweedie 1 1.005 0.1 note{Tweedie via mean, p, dispersion; variance = dispersion * mean**p.};
agg F.Signed dfreq [3] dsev [-2 5] [.5 .5] note{Signed severity -- negative outcomes allowed.};
agg F.Windowed 10_000 claims dsev [-1 1] poisson note{Windowed / discrete severity at high frequency.};
agg F.ApproxGamma 5000 claim sev lognorm 100 cv 2 poisson approximate sgamma note{Shifted-gamma moment approximation.};
agg F.ExactGamma 5000 claim sev lognorm 100 cv 2 poisson note{Exact computation}
